      "text": "First, we need to understand the relationship between \\(\\alpha\\) and \\(\\beta\\). Since \\(\\alpha\\) is inversely proportional to \\(\\beta\\), we can write the relationship as:\n\\[\n\\alpha \\beta = k\n\\]\nwhere \\(k\\) is a constant. To find the value of \\(k\\), we use the given values \\(\\alpha = 4\\) and \\(\\beta = 9\\):\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 9 = k \\implies k = 36\n\\]\nNow that we have the constant \\(k\\), we can use it to find \\(\\alpha\\) when \\(\\beta = -72\\). We substitute \\(\\beta = -72\\) and \\(k = 36\\) into the equation:\n\\[\n\\alpha \\cdot (-72) = 36\n\\]\nSolving for \\(\\alpha\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\alpha = \\frac{36}{-72} = -\\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\alpha\\) when \\(\\beta = -72\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]",
